From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: an out-of-context WinEvent hook on another process's thread needs no module

SetWinEventHook(..., NULL module, pid, tid, WINEVENT_OUTOFCONTEXT) on a thread of another process
works on Windows: the callback runs in the thread that set the hook. wineserver refused every
thread hook of another process without a module, which is right only for hooks that run in the
hooked thread. mpv embedded in SMPlayer (--wid) follows the size of SMPlayer's video widget this
way (EVENT_OBJECT_LOCATIONCHANGE); with the hook refused its picture kept the widget's first size,
491 of 654 pixels wide, the rest black, until something else resized it.

The UIPI check before it (no hooking an elevated program's thread from below) is unchanged.
---
--- a/server/hook.c
+++ b/server/hook.c
@@ -483,11 +483,19 @@
     }
     else
     {
-        /* module is optional only if hook is in current process */
+        /* module is optional only if hook is in current process -- or an out of
+         * context WinEvent hook, which runs in the thread that set it (Stained
+         * Glass OS, wine-sg 8403: mpv embedded in SMPlayer follows its parent
+         * window's size through EVENT_OBJECT_LOCATIONCHANGE from SMPlayer's thread;
+         * the hook was refused and mpv's picture kept its first size) */
         if (!module_size)
         {
             module = NULL;
-            if (thread->process != current->process)
+            if (thread->process != current->process
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_XPROC_WINEVENT
+                && (req->id != WH_WINEVENT || (req->flags & WINEVENT_INCONTEXT))
+#endif
+                )
             {
                 set_error( STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER );
                 goto done;
